  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759312,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 10th Frame: MSX - A Bowling Simulation\n\nStep onto the lanes with *10th Frame*, a realistic ten-pin bowling simulation for the MSX, published by Access Software in 1986. This sports title allows up to eight players to compete in either open bowling or a structured tournament, offering a blend of casual fun and strategic skill.\n\nExperience the thrill of the game from a behind-the-bowler 3D perspective, complete with a scorecard to track your progress. Before each game, customize your team with names and select individual player abilities: Kids (straight ball for beginners), Amateur, or Professional (requiring precision and control). A power meter, reminiscent of *Leaderboard*, dictates ball speed, while a hook zone allows for spin adjustments – mastering both is key to striking success.\n\nPrint scorecards to commemorate your victories! *10th Frame* delivers a challenging and rewarding bowling experience, praised for its slick programming and realistic simulation, making it a must-have for sports game enthusiasts on the MSX."
    },
